cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnyRoB in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AnyRoB: A highly customizable R Shiny web application for generating risk-of-bias traffic-light and summary plots for any assessment tool"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-15        # TODO: change to the day you publish the release
license: MIT                     # TODO: change if you chose a different licence for this repo
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/AnyRoB"     # TODO
url: "https://jonathanyuen.shinyapps.io/AnyRoB/"
abstract: >-
  AnyRoB is an R Shiny web application that generates highly customizable
  risk of bias traffic light and summary plots for any domain-based risk of
  bias assessment tool. Users define their own domains, subdomains and
  judgements (names, colours and symbols), enter assessments in the app or in
  Excel, and export publication-ready figures.
keywords:
  - risk of bias
  - systematic review
  - meta-analysis
  - traffic light plot
  - data visualization
  - R
  - Shiny
